  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas Asia Regional Anti-Trafficking Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas Asia have identified Safe Migration and Anti-trafficking as one of their programmatic strategic priorities in their new Regional Strategic Plan 2017-2020. This project builds on Caritas&apos; Asia&apos;s regional Anti-trafficking programme documented under GAS114 that began in 2014. Many Caritas agencies throughout Asia are working to prevent human trafficking and promote safe migration. This project will enhance the capacity of Caritas Asia member organisations (MOs) currently working on, or concerned with, human trafficking issues in their respective countries. The project aims to strengthen the national programs of Caritas MOs through regional and sub-regional needs-based training and workshops, sharing of experience and expertise across the region, and by strengthening networking and advocacy work. It will involve 24 member organisations across the region from Central, East, South and South East Asia.</narrative>
  </description>
